#
# names - plain words for packages: smoke add <word> looks a word up here when no recipe has
# that name. One entry per line: <word> <target> [<key fingerprint>]. The target is a cig
# recipe, or an upstream link (building from a link needs a generated recipe: planned).
# Your own entries go in /etc/smoke/names, which is read first. This file holds only the
# words for what cig itself needs; the full list will come online, signed by the cig
# project key (docs/smoke.md, "The name file").
#
# word          target
doas            opendoas
sh              busybox
coreutils       busybox
libc            musl
kernel          linux
firmware        linux-firmware
gnupg           gpgv
gpg             gpgv
init            sinit
mkfs.ext4       e2fsprogs
fdisk           util-linux
sfdisk          util-linux
smoke           cig-tools
cigbuild        cig-tools
